                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i][j - 1], dp[i - 1][j])

    return dp[n][n]
```

The `find_longest_repeating_subseq` function uses dynamic programming to solve the problem. It initializes a 2D list `dp` where `dp[i][j]` represents the length of the longest repeating subsequence of the first `i` characters of the string `s` that doesn't have the same character at the same position as the first `j` characters of the string `s`. The function iterates through each character of the string, comparing it with all previous characters to update the `dp` table accordingly. Finally, it returns the value at `dp[n][n]`, which represents the length of the longest repeating subsequence of the entire string `s` that meets the criteria.

